  <data name="Cleanup_Analyse" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Analizar oportunidades de limpieza</value>
    <comment>[button] Primary button in the Cleanup page header. Starts the read-only analysis that lists removable items; it deletes nothing.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_AutomationName" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Página de limpieza</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader name for the whole Cleanup page (the page reached from the Clean &gt; Cleanup navigation entry). Announced when the page gains focus.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Categories_Label" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Categorías que se incluirán</value>
    <comment>[label] Small label on the Cleanup page directly above the grouped list of cleanup category switches.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_BrowserCache_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Carpetas de caché de Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Brave y Opera.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line description under the 'Browser Cache' cleanup category on the Cleanup page. The user reads it to decide whether to let this category be deleted, so it must stay precise about what is removed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_BrowserCache_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Caché del navegador</value>
    <comment>[label] Name of one cleanup category in the grouped list on the Cleanup page, next to its on/off switch. It covers the cache folders of the installed web browsers; browser names are product names and stay as they are.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_CacheFolders_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Carpetas de caché en AppData que dejan varias aplicaciones.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line description under the 'Application Caches' cleanup category on the Cleanup page. The user reads it to decide whether to let this category be deleted, so it must stay precise about what is removed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_CacheFolders_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cachés de aplicaciones</value>
    <comment>[label] Name of one cleanup category in the grouped list on the Cleanup page, next to its on/off switch. It covers cache folders under AppData left behind by installed applications; AppData is a Windows folder name and stays as is.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_DeliveryOptimization_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Caché de uso compartido de Windows Update entre equipos.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line description under the 'Delivery Optimisation' cleanup category on the Cleanup page. The user reads it to decide whether to let this category be deleted, so it must stay precise about what is removed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_DeliveryOptimization_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Optimización de entrega</value>
    <comment>[label] Name of one cleanup category in the grouped list on the Cleanup page, next to its on/off switch. It covers the Windows feature that shares update downloads between PCs; use the name Windows itself uses in this language.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_DnsCache_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Vacía la caché de resolución DNS (ejecuta ipconfig /flushdns).</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line description under the 'DNS Client Cache' cleanup category on the Cleanup page. The user reads it to decide whether to let this category be deleted, so it must stay precise about what is removed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_DnsCache_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Caché del cliente DNS</value>
    <comment>[label] Name of one cleanup category in the grouped list on the Cleanup page, next to its on/off switch. It covers the DNS resolver cache; the command in brackets is a literal Windows command and stays as is.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_DownloadedInstallers_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Archivos de instalación (.exe, .msi, .iso …) en la carpeta Descargas.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line description under the 'Downloaded Installers' cleanup category on the Cleanup page. The user reads it to decide whether to let this category be deleted, so it must stay precise about what is removed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_DownloadedInstallers_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Instaladores descargados</value>
    <comment>[label] Name of one cleanup category in the grouped list on the Cleanup page, next to its on/off switch. It covers setup files left in the user's Downloads folder; the file extensions stay as they are.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_FontCache_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Caché de representación de fuentes. Se reconstruye en el próximo inicio.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line description under the 'Font Cache' cleanup category on the Cleanup page. The user reads it to decide whether to let this category be deleted, so it must stay precise about what is removed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_FontCache_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Caché de fuentes</value>
    <comment>[label] Name of one cleanup category in the grouped list on the Cleanup page, next to its on/off switch. It covers the font rendering cache, rebuilt the next time the PC starts.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_IconCache_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bases de datos de la caché de iconos del Explorador. Se reconstruyen automáticamente.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line description under the 'Icon Cache' cleanup category on the Cleanup page. The user reads it to decide whether to let this category be deleted, so it must stay precise about what is removed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_IconCache_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Caché de iconos</value>
    <comment>[label] Name of one cleanup category in the grouped list on the Cleanup page, next to its on/off switch. It covers File Explorer's cached icons, which Windows recreates by itself.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_LargeOldFiles_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Archivos que superan el umbral de tamaño y no se han modificado dentro del umbral de antigüedad.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line description under the 'Large &amp; Old Files' cleanup category on the Cleanup page. The user reads it to decide whether to let this category be deleted, so it must stay precise about what is removed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_LargeOldFiles_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Archivos grandes y antiguos</value>
    <comment>[label] Name of one cleanup category in the grouped list on the Cleanup page, next to its on/off switch. It covers the user's own files that are bigger than the size slider and older than the age slider on the same page.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_PrefetchFiles_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Datos de Prefetch del inicio de aplicaciones. Ligera ralentización tras la limpieza (requiere permisos de administrador).</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line description under the 'Prefetch Files' cleanup category on the Cleanup page. The user reads it to decide whether to let this category be deleted, so it must stay precise about what is removed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_PrefetchFiles_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Archivos de Prefetch</value>
    <comment>[label] Name of one cleanup category in the grouped list on the Cleanup page, next to its on/off switch. It covers the Windows Prefetch data that speeds up app start-up; removing it makes the next few starts slower and needs administrator rights.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_ProgramLeftovers_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Carpetas de AppData de programas desinstalados (más de 90 días sin actividad).</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line description under the 'Program Leftovers' cleanup category on the Cleanup page. The user reads it to decide whether to let this category be deleted, so it must stay precise about what is removed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_ProgramLeftovers_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Restos de programas</value>
    <comment>[label] Name of one cleanup category in the grouped list on the Cleanup page, next to its on/off switch. It covers AppData folders belonging to programs that are no longer installed and have not been touched for at least 90 days.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_RecycleBin_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Archivos que quedan en la Papelera de reciclaje de Windows.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line description under the 'Recycle Bin' cleanup category on the Cleanup page. The user reads it to decide whether to let this category be deleted, so it must stay precise about what is removed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_RecycleBin_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Papelera de reciclaje</value>
    <comment>[label] Name of one cleanup category in the grouped list on the Cleanup page, next to its on/off switch. It covers the Windows Recycle Bin itself; emptying it frees the space that deleted files still occupy.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_StoreLogs_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Registros de diagnóstico de Microsoft Store.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line description under the 'Microsoft Store Logs' cleanup category on the Cleanup page. The user reads it to decide whether to let this category be deleted, so it must stay precise about what is removed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_StoreLogs_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Registros de Microsoft Store</value>
    <comment>[label] Name of one cleanup category in the grouped list on the Cleanup page, next to its on/off switch. It covers diagnostic logs written by the Microsoft Store app; the product name stays as it is.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_TempFiles_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Carpetas Temp de Windows y archivos .tmp/.temp.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line description under the 'Temporary Files' cleanup category on the Cleanup page. The user reads it to decide whether to let this category be deleted, so it must stay precise about what is removed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_TempFiles_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Archivos temporales</value>
    <comment>[label] Name of one cleanup category in the grouped list on the Cleanup page, next to its on/off switch. It covers the Windows temporary folders and loose .tmp/.temp files.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_ThumbnailCache_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bases de datos de miniaturas del Explorador. Se reconstruyen cuando se necesitan.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line description under the 'Thumbnail Cache' cleanup category on the Cleanup page. The user reads it to decide whether to let this category be deleted, so it must stay precise about what is removed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_ThumbnailCache_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Caché de miniaturas</value>
    <comment>[label] Name of one cleanup category in the grouped list on the Cleanup page, next to its on/off switch. It covers File Explorer's cached preview images, which Windows recreates by itself.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_WindowsErrorReporting_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Registros de bloqueos y volcados de memoria de WER.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line description under the 'Error Reports &amp; Dumps' cleanup category on the Cleanup page. The user reads it to decide whether to let this category be deleted, so it must stay precise about what is removed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_WindowsErrorReporting_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Informes de errores y volcados</value>
    <comment>[label] Name of one cleanup category in the grouped list on the Cleanup page, next to its on/off switch. It covers Windows Error Reporting crash logs and memory dumps; WER is the Windows acronym and stays as is.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_WindowsUpdateCache_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Paquetes de actualización ya aplicados en SoftwareDistribution\Download.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line description under the 'Windows Update Cache' cleanup category on the Cleanup page. The user reads it to decide whether to let this category be deleted, so it must stay precise about what is removed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Category_WindowsUpdateCache_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Caché de Windows Update</value>
    <comment>[label] Name of one cleanup category in the grouped list on the Cleanup page, next to its on/off switch. It covers update packages Windows already installed; the folder path stays untranslated.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_DryRun_Checkbox" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Simulación (solo vista previa)</value>
    <comment>[label] Checkbox next to the Cleanup page's execute button. When ticked the cleanup is simulated and nothing is deleted.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Group_Applications" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Aplicaciones</value>
    <comment>[header] Name of the collapsible group on the Cleanup page holding the categories for leftovers of installed applications.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Group_Browsers" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Navegadores</value>
    <comment>[header] Name of the collapsible group on the Cleanup page holding the web-browser cleanup categories.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Group_Downloads" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Descargas e instaladores</value>
    <comment>[header] Name of the collapsible group on the Cleanup page holding the categories for the user's Downloads folder and downloaded installer files.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Group_Files" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Archivos y almacenamiento</value>
    <comment>[header] Name of the collapsible group on the Cleanup page holding the categories that work on the user's own files, such as large and old files.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Group_WindowsSystem" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Sistema de Windows</value>
    <comment>[header] Name of the collapsible group on the Cleanup page holding the Windows-provided cleanup categories (temp files, update cache, caches, and so on).</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_LargeFileThreshold_Label" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Umbral de archivo grande: {0} MB</value>
    <comment>[label] Caption above the slider on the Cleanup page that sets the size from which a file counts as large. {0} is an already-formatted number such as '500'; MB is the unit and is not translated.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_OldFileAge_Label" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Umbral de antigüedad: {0} días</value>
    <comment>[label] Caption above the slider on the Cleanup page that sets how long a file must have been untouched to count as old. {0} is an already-formatted number such as '365'.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Options_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Opciones de limpieza</value>
    <comment>[header] Header of the card on the Cleanup page that holds the deletion-mode switches and the list of cleanup categories.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Policy_Admin" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>administrador</value>
    <comment>[label] One flag in the comma-separated policy list shown on a suggestion row on the Cleanup page. Means the suggestion needs administrator rights. Lower case because the flags are joined into one line.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Policy_NoPermanentDelete" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>sin eliminación definitiva</value>
    <comment>[label] One flag in the comma-separated policy list on a suggestion row on the Cleanup page. Means this suggestion cannot be deleted permanently, only the recoverable paths are available. Lower case because the flags are joined into one line.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Policy_NoQuarantine" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>sin cuarentena</value>
    <comment>[label] One flag in the comma-separated policy list on a suggestion row on the Cleanup page. Means this suggestion cannot be quarantined for later restore. Lower case because the flags are joined into one line.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Policy_NoRecycleBin" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>sin Papelera de reciclaje</value>
    <comment>[label] One flag in the comma-separated policy list on a suggestion row on the Cleanup page. Means this suggestion cannot be routed through the Recycle Bin. Lower case because the flags are joined into one line.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Policy_ServiceStop" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>parada de servicio</value>
    <comment>[label] One flag in the comma-separated policy list on a suggestion row on the Cleanup page. Means a Windows service has to be stopped before the files can be removed. Lower case because the flags are joined into one line.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Policy_Standard" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>directiva estándar</value>
    <comment>[label] Shown in place of the flag list on a suggestion row on the Cleanup page when no special handling applies. Lower case, same position as the flag list.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Progress_Cleaning" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Limpiando…</value>
    <comment>[status] Progress caption above the progress bar on the Cleanup page while a real cleanup is in progress.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Progress_Complete" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Limpieza completada.</value>
    <comment>[status] Progress caption on the Cleanup page when a real cleanup run has finished.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Progress_DryRun" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ejecutando la vista previa de simulación…</value>
    <comment>[status] Progress caption above the progress bar on the Cleanup page while a dry run (simulation) is in progress.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Progress_Item" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Elemento {0} de {1}: {2}</value>
    <comment>[status] Progress caption above the progress bar on the Cleanup page, naming the item being processed. {0} is the current item number, {1} the total, {2} the item's title.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Progress_PreviewComplete" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Vista previa completada.</value>
    <comment>[status] Progress caption on the Cleanup page when a dry run has finished. Nothing was deleted.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_RunPreview_Button" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ejecutar vista previa</value>
    <comment>[button] Confirm button of the dry-run confirmation dialog on the Cleanup page. Starts the simulation; deletes nothing.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_SelectedTotal_Label" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Seleccionado</value>
    <comment>[label] Small label above the total size of the currently ticked suggestions, in the bar at the bottom of the Cleanup page. The value below it is a size such as '1.2 GB'.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Session_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>La limpieza parte de un análisis completado para que las recomendaciones sigan siendo explicables y reversibles de forma predeterminada.</value>
    <comment>[description] Helper text under the 'Select scan session' header on the Cleanup page, explaining why a finished scan has to be chosen first.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Session_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Seleccionar sesión de análisis</value>
    <comment>[header] Header of the card on the Cleanup page holding the drop-down that picks which completed scan the cleanup suggestions are based on.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Status_Analysing" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Analizando…</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Cleanup page while the read-only analysis is running. The trailing ellipsis marks it as an ongoing operation.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Status_AnalysisCancelled" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Análisis cancelado. Revise la sesión y las opciones seleccionadas y vuelva a intentarlo.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Cleanup page after the analysis was cancelled, usually because the user changed the session or the options while it ran.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Status_AnalysisFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error en el análisis: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Cleanup page when the analysis threw an error. {0} is the underlying technical error text, which stays English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Status_CleanupFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error en la limpieza: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line and result summary on the Cleanup page when the cleanup run itself threw an error. {0} is the underlying technical error text, which stays English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Status_Found" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Se han encontrado {0} sugerencias. Seleccione los elementos que se van a limpiar.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Cleanup page after a successful analysis. {0} is the number of suggestions; the English uses '(s)' to cover singular and plural, so use whatever form is natural in the target language.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Status_Initial" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Seleccione una sesión de análisis y analice para ver las sugerencias.</value>
    <comment>[status] First status line on the Cleanup page, shown before the user has run an analysis.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Status_InitializationFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error al inicializar la limpieza: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Cleanup page when the page could not load its scan sessions or settings. {0} is the underlying technical error text, which stays English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Status_NoOpportunities" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No se han encontrado oportunidades de limpieza para este análisis.</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Status line on the Cleanup page when the analysis finished but found nothing worth removing.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Status_ReportUnavailable" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>La interfaz de limpieza no pudo mostrar un resultado confirmado: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Cleanup page when the run finished but the result dialog could not be shown. {0} is the underlying technical error text, which stays English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Status_ScopeChanged" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>El ámbito de la limpieza ha cambiado. Vuelva a analizar antes de limpiar.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Cleanup page after the user changed the session, the deletion mode, a category or a threshold. The previous results were discarded and a fresh analysis is required.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Status_SessionUnavailable" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>La sesión de análisis {0} no está completada o ya no existe. Seleccione una sesión completada.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Cleanup page when the page was opened for a specific scan that has since been removed or never finished. {0} is the numeric scan id.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Subtitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Previsualice los candidatos de limpieza recuperables antes de cualquier operación destructiva.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line description under the Cleanup page title. Tells the user the page first shows what could be removed and deletes nothing on its own.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Suggestion_Confidence" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} de confianza</value>
    <comment>[label] Small caption on each suggestion row on the Cleanup page, showing how sure the analysis is. {0} is an already-formatted percentage such as '85 %'.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Suggestions_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Sugerencias</value>
    <comment>[header] Header above the list of individual cleanup suggestions produced by the analysis on the Cleanup page.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Cleanup_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Limpieza</value>
    <comment>[title] Heading at the top of the Cleanup page. Same word as the Nav_Cleanup navigation entry but rendered as the page's own large title; keep the two consistent.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Common_Cancel" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cancelar</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Common_Close" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cerrar</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Common_Delete" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Eliminar</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Common_Free" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>libre</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Common_Healthy" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Correcto</value>
  </data>
