    <value>Examinar…</value>
    <comment>[button] Button beside the path box on the Scan page that opens the Windows folder picker. Ends with an ellipsis character because it opens a dialog.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Calculating" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Calculando</value>
    <comment>[status] Placeholder shown in the Speed, File rate and ETA readouts of the live progress panel until enough of the scan has run to measure them.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Complete_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Análisis completado. Espacio de trabajo listo.</value>
    <comment>[title] Heading of the green banner at the bottom of the Scan page after a scan finishes. "Workspace" is the app page holding the scan results.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_DeepScan_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Intenta acceder a las carpetas protegidas, desactiva las exclusiones del sistema predeterminadas y registra los errores de acceso denegado en lugar de omitirlos en silencio. Se recomienda el modo administrador.</value>
    <comment>[description] Helper paragraph under the Deep Scan toggle on the Scan page, spelling out what deep scanning changes.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Elevation_Button" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ejecutar como administrador</value>
    <comment>[button] Button in the amber warning panel on the Scan page that restarts the scan in a separate process with Windows administrator rights.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Elevation_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Sin permisos de administrador se registrarán errores de acceso denegado en las carpetas protegidas del sistema. Use el botón para reiniciar la aplicación con todos los privilegios.</value>
    <comment>[description] Body of the amber warning panel on the Scan page, explaining what happens without administrator rights. "The button" is the Scan_Elevation_Button beside this text.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Elevation_Failed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No se pudo iniciar el proceso de análisis con privilegios elevados.</value>
    <comment>[status] Error shown on the Scan page when the request for administrator rights was refused or the second process could not be started.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Elevation_Started" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>El análisis profundo con privilegios elevados se ha iniciado en un proceso de línea de comandos independiente. Actualice Resultados cuando finalice.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Scan page after the user chooses "Run as Administrator". The scan then runs in a second, elevated process, so this page cannot show its progress. "Results" names the app page the user should refresh.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Elevation_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Se recomiendan privilegios de administrador</value>
    <comment>[title] Heading of the amber warning panel on the Scan page shown when deep scan is on but the app does not have Windows administrator rights.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Error_FolderPickerFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No se pudo abrir el selector de carpetas: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Error banner on the Scan page when the Windows folder-picker dialog could not be opened. {0} is the technical error detail, which stays in English by policy - translate only the sentence before it and keep the colon.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Error_InitializeFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No se pudo inicializar la página de análisis: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Error banner on the Scan page when the page itself could not load its drives or settings. {0} is the technical error detail, which stays in English by policy - translate only the sentence before it and keep the colon.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Error_NoDetails" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>El analizador notificó un error sin detalles adicionales.</value>
    <comment>[status] Error text on the Scan page when the scan failed but gave no reason of its own.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Error_NonTerminalStatus" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>El analizador devolvió el estado no final {0}.</value>
    <comment>[status] Error text on the Scan page for an internal fault: the scanner came back while still claiming to be in progress. {0} is an untranslated status word.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Eta_Estimating" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Estimando…</value>
    <comment>[status] Value of the "ETA" readout in the live progress panel before the scan has run long enough to predict a finish time. Ends with an ellipsis character.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Eta_Finalizing" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Finalizando</value>
    <comment>[status] Value of the "ETA" readout once every expected byte has been read and the scan is writing its results.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Eta_NoSubtreeEstimate" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Sin estimación para una carpeta</value>
    <comment>[status] Value of the "ETA" readout when only part of a drive is being scanned. The app refuses to guess a finish time because it does not know how big that folder is. "Subtree" means a folder rather than a whole drive.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Failed_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error en el análisis</value>
    <comment>[title] Heading of the red banner at the bottom of the Scan page when a scan ends in an error. The detail underneath comes from the scanner.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_FileRate_PerMinute" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} archivos/min</value>
    <comment>[status] Value of the "File rate" readout in the live progress panel when the scan is processing less than one file per second. {0} is a formatted number. Keep the per-minute unit short - it sits in a narrow column.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_FileRate_PerSecond" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} archivos/s</value>
    <comment>[status] Value of the "File rate" readout in the live progress panel at normal speeds. {0} is a formatted number. Keep the per-second unit short - it sits in a narrow column.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Metric_Elapsed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Transcurrido</value>
    <comment>[label] Caption over the time the running scan has taken so far, in the live progress panel.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Metric_Errors" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Errores</value>
    <comment>[label] Caption over the count of files and folders the scan could not read, in the live progress panel shown while a scan runs.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Metric_Eta" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Tiempo restante</value>
    <comment>[label] Caption over the estimated time still remaining, in the live progress panel. English uses the abbreviation; use whatever short form is normal in the target language.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Metric_FileRate" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Tasa de archivos</value>
    <comment>[label] Caption over how many files per second or per minute the scan is processing, in the live progress panel. Shown next to Speed because byte throughput alone is misleading for many small files.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Metric_Files" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Archivos</value>
    <comment>[label] Caption over the running count of files found so far, in the live progress panel shown while a scan runs.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Metric_Folders" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Carpetas</value>
    <comment>[label] Caption over the running count of folders visited so far, in the live progress panel shown while a scan runs.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Metric_Size" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Tamaño</value>
    <comment>[label] Caption over the total size measured so far (for example "4.20 GB"), in the live progress panel shown while a scan runs.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Metric_Speed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Velocidad</value>
    <comment>[label] Caption over the current throughput in bytes per second, in the live progress panel shown while a scan runs.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Mode_Custom" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Análisis personalizado</value>
    <comment>[label] Title of the fourth of four clickable scan-mode tiles on the Scan page, and the heading shown over the options once that mode is picked. Uses whatever the user has already configured.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Mode_Custom_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Usa las opciones actuales de esta página y las exclusiones guardadas.</value>
    <comment>[description] Explanation under the "Custom Scan" tile title on the Scan page. "Toggles" are the switches on this page; "exclusions" are folders the user has excluded in Settings.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Mode_Deep" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Análisis profundo</value>
    <comment>[label] Name of the most thorough scan mode. Used in three places on the Scan page: the third of four mode tiles, the heading over the options once it is picked, and the label of the toggle that switches deep scanning on.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Mode_Deep_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Carpetas protegidas y registro de accesos denegados.</value>
    <comment>[description] Explanation under the "Deep Scan" tile title on the Scan page. Means the mode enters protected folders and reports what it could not read.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Mode_Quick" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Análisis rápido</value>
    <comment>[label] Title of the first of four clickable scan-mode tiles on the Scan page, and the heading shown over the options once that mode is picked. The fastest mode.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Mode_Quick_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Lectura rápida de metadatos para la revisión habitual del almacenamiento.</value>
    <comment>[description] Explanation under the "Quick Scan" tile title on the Scan page.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Mode_Standard" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Análisis estándar</value>
    <comment>[label] Title of the second of four clickable scan-mode tiles on the Scan page, and the heading shown over the options once that mode is picked. This is the default mode.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Mode_Standard_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Equilibrio recomendado para los análisis rutinarios de unidades.</value>
    <comment>[description] Explanation under the "Standard Scan" tile title on the Scan page.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_PathError_DriveNotReady" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>La unidad seleccionada no está lista.</value>
    <comment>[status] Validation message under the path box on the Scan page when the drive exists but cannot be read - for example an empty card reader or a disconnected mapped drive.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_PathError_Empty" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Elija una carpeta o unidad para analizar.</value>
    <comment>[status] Validation message under the path box on the Scan page when the box is empty. Blocks the Start Scan button.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_PathError_Missing" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>La ruta de análisis no existe o no está disponible actualmente.</value>
    <comment>[status] Validation message under the path box on the Scan page when the typed folder cannot be found - it may have been deleted, or sit on a disconnected network share.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_PathError_NotAbsolute" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>La ruta de análisis debe ser una ruta absoluta de Windows.</value>
    <comment>[status] Validation message under the path box on the Scan page when the typed path is relative. An absolute path starts with a drive letter or a network share.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_PathError_PreflightFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error en la comprobación previa al inicio: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Validation message under the path box on the Scan page when the app cannot write to its own data folder, so no scan could be saved. {0} is the technical error detail, which stays in English by policy - translate only the sentence before it and keep the colon.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Path_Placeholder" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>p. ej. C:\ o C:\Users</value>
    <comment>[placeholder] Grey hint text inside the empty path box on the Scan page. The two Windows paths are examples and must stay exactly as they are; translate only the "e.g." part.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Progress_Cancelled" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Análisis cancelado.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Scan page progress panel after the user stops a running scan. Has a closing full stop, unlike the Scan_Step_Cancelled wayfinding line.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Progress_Complete" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Análisis completado — {0} en {1} archivos</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line summarising a finished scan, shown in the progress panel and repeated in the green completion banner. {0} is a formatted size such as "4.20 GB"; {1} is a formatted file count. The dash is an em dash. No closing full stop in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Progress_DidNotComplete" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>El análisis no se completó.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Scan page progress panel for the rare case where the scanner returns without either finishing, failing or being cancelled.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Progress_Failed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error en el análisis.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Scan page progress panel when a scan ends in an error. Has a closing full stop, unlike the Scan_Step_Failed wayfinding line.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Progress_Preparing" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Preparando el análisis...</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the live progress panel between pressing Start Scan and the first file being counted. English uses three full stops rather than an ellipsis character.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Progress_Running" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} analizados · {1} archivos</value>
    <comment>[status] Live status line above the progress bar while a scan runs. {0} is a formatted size such as "1.4 GB", {1} a formatted file count. The separator is a middle dot with a space on each side.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_SelectPath_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Seleccione la ruta para analizar</value>
    <comment>[header] Section heading over the path text box, Browse button and drive shortcut buttons on the Scan page.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Start" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Iniciar análisis</value>
    <comment>[button] Primary button that begins a scan. Appears in the Scan page header and again as the primary action in the Dashboard page header, where it opens the Scan page. Both places use this one string.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Step1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Paso 1 de 4 · Elegir qué analizar</value>
    <comment>[status] Wayfinding line under the Scan page heading while the user is still picking what to scan. The separator is a middle dot with a space on each side. "Scope" means the folder or drive to scan.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Step2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Paso 2 de 4 · Elegir el modo de análisis</value>
    <comment>[status] Wayfinding line under the Scan page heading after the user picks one of the four scan-mode tiles. The separator is a middle dot with a space on each side.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Step3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Paso 3 de 4 · Ejecutar el análisis</value>
    <comment>[status] Wayfinding line under the Scan page heading while a scan is running. The separator is a middle dot with a space on each side.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Step4" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Paso 4 de 4 · Revisar los resultados</value>
    <comment>[status] Wayfinding line under the Scan page heading once a scan has finished successfully. The separator is a middle dot with a space on each side.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Step_Cancelled" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Análisis cancelado</value>
    <comment>[status] Replaces the "Step n of 4" wayfinding line under the Scan page heading when the user stops a running scan. No closing full stop, unlike Scan_Progress_Cancelled.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Step_Failed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error en el análisis</value>
    <comment>[status] Replaces the "Step n of 4" wayfinding line under the Scan page heading when a scan ends in an error. No closing full stop; kept separate from the Scan_Failed_Title banner heading so the short line can be shortened independently.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Análisis</value>
    <comment>[title] Main heading at the top of the Scan page. Separate from the "Scan" entry in the left navigation rail (Nav_Scan) so page heading and rail entry can be worded independently.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Turbo_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Usa un motor nativo de Rust con recorrido paralelo por robo de trabajo, mucho más rápido en unidades NVMe/SSD con muchos archivos. Si no se encuentra el binario del motor, recurre automáticamente al analizador administrado.</value>
    <comment>[description] Helper paragraph under the Turbo Scanner toggle on the Scan page. Rust, NVMe and SSD are not translated. "Managed scanner" means the built-in .NET one.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Turbo_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Turbo Scanner (basado en Rust)</value>
    <comment>[header] Label of the toggle that switches on the optional native scanning engine on the Scan page. "Turbo Scanner" is the feature name and "Rust" is the programming language; neither is translated.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Turbo_Missing_Message" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No se encontró turbo-scanner.exe junto a la aplicación. Compílelo desde el código fuente o instale una versión de lanzamiento para habilitar esta función.</value>
    <comment>[description] Body of the warning banner on the Scan page when the optional engine is missing. turbo-scanner.exe is a filename and stays exactly as written.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_Turbo_Missing_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No se encontró el binario de Turbo Scanner</value>
    <comment>[title] Heading of the warning banner on the Scan page shown when the optional turbo-scanner program is not installed beside the app.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Scan_ViewResults" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ver resultados</value>
    <comment>[button] Button in the Scan page header, shown only after a scan finishes. Opens the workspace with that scan's results. "Results" refers to the app page of that name.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_About_Tagline" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Analizador de uso de disco y herramienta de limpieza para Windows.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line description of the product in the About block of the Advanced Diagnostics and About settings category, under the product name and version.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_About_VersionLabel" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Versión </value>
    <comment>[label] Static run of text in the Advanced Diagnostics and About settings category, immediately followed by the version number on the same line, under the product name. KEEP THE TRAILING SPACE - it is the gap before the number.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Accent_Aurora" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Aurora — verde azulado</value>
    <comment>[label] One entry in the accent-colour picker in Settings. "Aurora" is the theme's own name and stays as is; the part after the dash names the colour (teal). Separator is an em dash.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Accent_AutomationHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Color de énfasis usado para resaltar y seleccionar. Se comprueba el contraste de todos los colores de énfasis en ambos temas.</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader help text for the accent-colour dropdown in General and Appearance settings. Not shown on screen.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Accent_AutomationName" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Color de énfasis</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader name for the accent-colour dropdown in General and Appearance settings. Not shown on screen.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Accent_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Se aplica de inmediato. Los colores de gravedad no cambian, de modo que una advertencia siempre se reconoce como tal.</value>
    <comment>[description] Helper sentence under the accent-colour dropdown in General and Appearance settings. Explains that changing the accent needs no restart and does not repaint the fixed warning/error colours.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Accent_Ember" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ember — ámbar</value>
    <comment>[label] One entry in the accent-colour picker in Settings. "Ember" is the theme's own name and stays as is; the part after the dash names the colour (amber). Separator is an em dash.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Accent_Label" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Color de énfasis</value>
    <comment>[label] Caption above the accent-colour dropdown in the General and Appearance settings category. Windows calls this the accent colour.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Accent_Verdant" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Verdant — verde</value>
    <comment>[label] One entry in the accent-colour picker in Settings. "Verdant" is the theme's own name and stays as is; the part after the dash names the colour (green). Separator is an em dash.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Accent_Violet" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Violet — morado</value>
    <comment>[label] One entry in the accent-colour picker in Settings. "Violet" is the theme's own name and stays as is; the part after the dash names the colour (purple). Separator is an em dash.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Category_AdvancedDiagnostics_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Exportación de diagnóstico e información de versión.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line subtitle under the "Advanced Diagnostics &amp; About" card on the Settings hub, listing what the category contains. Also matched against the Settings search box.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Category_AdvancedDiagnostics_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Diagnóstico avanzado y Acerca de</value>
    <comment>[title] Title of the "Advanced Diagnostics &amp; About" card on the Settings hub, and the heading of that category's editor pane once it is opened. Groups the settings for exporting a diagnostics bundle and viewing the installed version.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Category_Cleanup_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Comportamiento de eliminación, umbrales y reglas predeterminadas.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line subtitle under the "Cleanup &amp; Safety" card on the Settings hub, listing what the category contains. Also matched against the Settings search box.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Category_Cleanup_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Limpieza y seguridad</value>
    <comment>[title] Title of the "Cleanup &amp; Safety" card on the Settings hub, and the heading of that category's editor pane once it is opened. Groups the settings for whether deletions go to the Recycle Bin, size/age thresholds, and which cleanup rules are on by default.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Category_Duplicates_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Métodos de detección, archivo que se conserva y FFmpeg.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line subtitle under the "Duplicates &amp; Matching" card on the Settings hub, listing what the category contains. Also matched against the Settings search box.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Category_Duplicates_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Duplicados y coincidencias</value>
    <comment>[title] Title of the "Duplicates &amp; Matching" card on the Settings hub, and the heading of that category's editor pane once it is opened. Groups the settings for which duplicate-detection methods run, which copy is kept, and the FFmpeg path.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Category_General_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Tema, densidad, página de inicio y ruta de análisis.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line subtitle under the "General &amp; Appearance" card on the Settings hub, listing what the category contains. Also matched against the Settings search box.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Category_General_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>General y apariencia</value>
    <comment>[title] Title of the "General &amp; Appearance" card on the Settings hub, and the heading of that category's editor pane once it is opened. Groups the settings for theme, UI density, which page the app opens on, and the folder scans start from.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Category_ResultsHistory_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Retención del historial y tamaño de página predeterminado.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line subtitle under the "Results &amp; History" card on the Settings hub, listing what the category contains. Also matched against the Settings search box.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Category_ResultsHistory_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Resultados e historial</value>
    <comment>[title] Title of the "Results &amp; History" card on the Settings hub, and the heading of that category's editor pane once it is opened. Groups the settings for how long scan history is kept and how many rows a results page shows.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Category_Scanning_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Paralelismo, archivos ocultos, exclusiones y retención.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line subtitle under the "Scanning &amp; Performance" card on the Settings hub, listing what the category contains. Also matched against the Settings search box.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Category_Scanning_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Análisis y rendimiento</value>
    <comment>[title] Title of the "Scanning &amp; Performance" card on the Settings hub, and the heading of that category's editor pane once it is opened. Groups the settings for scan thread count, whether hidden files are included, excluded folders, and how long history is kept.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Category_Scheduling_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Análisis programados, trabajos de limpieza y desencadenadores.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line subtitle under the "Scheduling &amp; Automation" card on the Settings hub, listing what the category contains. Also matched against the Settings search box.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Category_Scheduling_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Programación y automatización</value>
    <comment>[title] Title of the "Scheduling &amp; Automation" card on the Settings hub, and the heading of that category's editor pane once it is opened. Groups the settings for scans and cleanup jobs that run automatically on a schedule.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Category_TrayNotifications_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Minimizar al área de notificación, inicio y alertas de poco espacio.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line subtitle under the "Background, Tray &amp; Notifications" card on the Settings hub, listing what the category contains. Also matched against the Settings search box.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Category_TrayNotifications_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Segundo plano, área de notificación y alertas</value>
