  <data name="Settings_SkipSystemFolders_AutomationHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Omite los directorios Windows y Program Files para evitar inestabilidad.</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader help text for the Skip system folders switch in Scanning and Performance settings. Windows and Program Files are literal folder names and stay in English. Not shown on screen.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_SkipSystemFolders_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Omitir carpetas del sistema</value>
    <comment>[header] Label of an on/off switch in the Scanning and Performance settings category. Also used as that switch's screen-reader name.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_StartTrayOnLogin_AutomationHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Inicia StorageMaster automáticamente al iniciar sesión.</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader help text for the start-on-sign-in switch. Not shown on screen.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_StartTrayOnLogin_AutomationName" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Iniciar en el área de notificación al iniciar sesión</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader name for the start-on-sign-in switch. Shorter than the visible label. Not shown on screen.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_StartTrayOnLogin_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Iniciar en el área de notificación al iniciar sesión en Windows</value>
    <comment>[header] Label of an on/off switch in the Background, Tray and Notifications settings category. Sign-in should use the same wording Windows uses for logging in.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Summary_Duplicates" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Conservar {0} · mín. {1} MB</value>
    <comment>[status] Status badge on the "Duplicates &amp; Matching" card on the Settings hub. {0} is the keeper policy (which copy of a duplicate set is kept, e.g. Newest); {1} is the smallest file size in megabytes that duplicate detection considers.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Summary_ResultsHistory" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} días de retención</value>
    <comment>[status] Status badge on the "Results &amp; History" card on the Settings hub. {0} is the number of days scan history is kept before it can be purged.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Summary_Scanning" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} subprocesos · {1} exclusiones</value>
    <comment>[status] Status badge on the "Scanning &amp; Performance" card on the Settings hub. {0} is the number of scan threads, {1} the number of excluded folders. The separator is a middle dot.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Summary_Scheduling" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} trabajo(s)</value>
    <comment>[status] Status badge on the "Scheduling &amp; Automation" card on the Settings hub. {0} is how many scheduled jobs exist. English uses "(s)" to cover 0, 1 and many; use whatever plural form reads naturally in the target language.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Summary_TrayDisabled" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Área de notificación desactivada</value>
    <comment>[status] Status badge on the "Background, Tray &amp; Notifications" card on the Settings hub, shown when the app does not minimise to the Windows notification area.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Summary_TrayEnabled" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Área de notificación activada</value>
    <comment>[status] Status badge on the "Background, Tray &amp; Notifications" card on the Settings hub, shown when closing the window minimises the app to the Windows notification area.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Summary_UpdatesAutoCheck" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Búsqueda automática</value>
    <comment>[status] Status badge on the "Updates &amp; Security" card on the Settings hub, shown when the app checks for a new version automatically at startup.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Summary_UpdatesManual" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Búsqueda manual</value>
    <comment>[status] Status badge on the "Updates &amp; Security" card on the Settings hub, shown when the user has to press the check-for-updates button themselves.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Theme_AutomationHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Elegir Claro, Oscuro o Predeterminado para seguir la configuración de Windows.</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader help text for the theme dropdown in General and Appearance settings. Light, Dark and Default are the dropdown's own entries. Not shown on screen.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Theme_Label" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Tema</value>
    <comment>[label] Caption above the light/dark theme dropdown in the General and Appearance settings category. Also used as that dropdown's screen-reader name.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Configuración</value>
    <comment>[title] Fallback title shown at the top of the Settings editor pane when no known category is selected. Same word as the Settings entry in the app's navigation rail.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_UiDensity_AutomationHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Compacta muestra más contenido. Cómoda añade más espaciado.</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader help text for the interface-density dropdown in General and Appearance settings. Compact and Comfortable are the dropdown's own entries. Not shown on screen.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_UiDensity_Label" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Densidad de la interfaz</value>
    <comment>[label] Caption above the interface-density dropdown (Compact / Comfortable) in the General and Appearance settings category. Also used as that dropdown's screen-reader name.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_UninstallPreservesData_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>La desinstalación desde el instalador ahora conserva de forma predeterminada la base de datos y la configuración en %LOCALAPPDATA%\StorageMaster.</value>
    <comment>[description] Footnote at the bottom of the Results and History settings category. %LOCALAPPDATA% is a Windows environment variable and StorageMaster is the product name; keep the whole path exactly as written.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Update_Available" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Hay disponible una actualización a la versión {0}.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Updates section of Settings after a check found a newer release. {0} is the new version number.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Update_AvailableDetail" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>La versión {0} está disponible  (publicada el {1})</value>
    <comment>[description] Line describing the newer StorageMaster release found by the update check, shown in the Updates section of Settings. {0} is the version number, {1} the release date already formatted for the user's locale. Note the two spaces before the bracket in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Update_CheckFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error al buscar actualizaciones: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Updates section of Settings when the update check itself could not be completed. {0} is the technical error text, which stays in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Update_Checking" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Buscando actualizaciones…</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Updates section of Settings while the app is contacting GitHub to look for a newer release. Ends with an ellipsis character.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Update_DownloadCancelled" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Descarga cancelada.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Updates section of Settings after the user pressed the cancel button during the update download.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Update_DownloadFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error en la descarga: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Updates section of Settings for any other update-download failure. {0} is the technical error text, which stays in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Update_DownloadFailed_Checksum" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error en la descarga: la suma de comprobación no coincide. Inténtelo de nuevo.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Updates section of Settings when the downloaded installer's checksum did not match the published one, so it was discarded.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Update_DownloadFailed_FileInUse" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error en la descarga: otro proceso tiene bloqueado el archivo del instalador. Cierre los instaladores abiertos e inténtelo de nuevo.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Updates section of Settings when the update installer file on disk is held open by another program and could not be written.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Update_DownloadFailed_InsecureUrl" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error en la descarga: el actualizador rechazó una dirección de descarga que no usa HTTPS.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Updates section of Settings when the download address was not HTTPS, so the updater refused to fetch it.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Update_DownloadFailed_MissingAsset" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error en la descarga: falta el instalador en la versión publicada.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Updates section of Settings when the published release does not contain an installer file to download.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Update_DownloadFailed_Signature" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error en la descarga: no se pudo verificar la confianza del instalador.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Updates section of Settings when the downloaded installer's signature could not be trusted, so it was discarded.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Update_DownloadFailed_Timeout" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error en la descarga: se agotó el tiempo de espera de la red al obtener el archivo de la versión.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Updates section of Settings when the connection to the release server timed out during the download.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Update_DownloadProgress" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Descargando… {0:F0}%</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Updates section of Settings next to the progress bar while the installer downloads. {0:F0} is the percentage complete, rounded to a whole number; keep the :F0 part exactly as it is.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Update_Downloading" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Descargando la actualización…</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Updates section of Settings while the installer is being downloaded, before the first progress percentage arrives. Ends with an ellipsis character.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Update_ElevationCancelled" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Se canceló el inicio del instalador en la solicitud de elevación de permisos.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Updates section of Settings when the user dismissed the Windows administrator-permission prompt, so the update installer never started.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Update_LaunchFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No se pudo iniciar el instalador. Ejecútelo manualmente desde %TEMP%\StorageMaster\Updates\.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Updates section of Settings when the downloaded installer could not be started. The path is a literal Windows folder location and must not be translated.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Update_LaunchingInstaller" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Iniciando el instalador…</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Updates section of Settings after the download finished, while the downloaded installer is being started. Ends with an ellipsis character.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Update_None" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Actualmente no hay ninguna actualización compatible disponible.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Updates section of Settings after a check found nothing newer to install.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Update_ReadyToDownload" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>La actualización a la versión {0} está lista para descargarse.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Updates section of Settings when the page opens and a previously found update is waiting. {0} is the new version number.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_UseTurboScanner_AutomationHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Usa el analizador nativo escrito en Rust cuando está disponible junto al ejecutable.</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader help text for the Use Turbo Scanner switch in Scanning and Performance settings. Rust is a programming language name and stays in English. Not shown on screen.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_UseTurboScanner_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Usar Turbo Scanner de forma predeterminada</value>
    <comment>[header] Label of an on/off switch in the Scanning and Performance settings category. Turbo Scanner is the name of the bundled native scanner component. Also used as that switch's screen-reader name.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Validation_FixErrors" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Corrija los errores de validación antes de guardar.</value>
    <comment>[status] Message shown in the Settings editor when the user presses Save while a field (scan path or FFmpeg path) still has an error.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Version_Unknown" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Desconocida</value>
    <comment>[label] Shown in place of the installed StorageMaster version number on the About section of Settings when the version cannot be read from the running program.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_VideoFrameThreshold_AutomationHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Número de fotogramas muestreados que se comparan para determinar la similitud de vídeo.</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader help text for the video frame threshold spin box in Duplicates and Matching settings. Not shown on screen.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_VideoFrameThreshold_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Umbral de fotogramas de vídeo</value>
    <comment>[header] Header of a numeric spin box in Duplicates and Matching settings controlling how many sampled video frames are compared. Also used as that spin box's screen-reader name.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_VideoPerceptualReview_AutomationHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Agrupa vídeos visualmente similares mediante hashes de fotogramas. Requiere FFmpeg y ffprobe.</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader help text for the video perceptual review switch in Duplicates and Matching settings. FFmpeg and ffprobe are external tool names and are never translated. Not shown on screen.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_VideoPerceptualReview_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Activar revisión perceptual de vídeos</value>
    <comment>[header] Label of an on/off switch in Duplicates and Matching settings. Turns on grouping of visually similar videos. Also used as that switch's screen-reader name.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_ViewReleaseNotes" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ver las notas de la versión en GitHub</value>
    <comment>[button] Link inside the highlighted panel that appears when a newer version is available. Opens the release page in the browser. GitHub is never translated.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Warning_SignedUpdatesRecommended" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Por seguridad, se recomienda usar actualizaciones firmadas.</value>
    <comment>[description] Warning shown on the "Updates &amp; Security" card on the Settings hub when the user has turned off the requirement that update installers carry a valid signature.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_DiskMonitorStarting" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Iniciando la supervisión de disco</value>
    <comment>[status] Line in the 'Global status' box at the bottom of the navigation rail. Shown while the background free-space monitor is doing its first pass; replaced by Shell_DrivesHealthy or Shell_LowestFreeSpace afterwards. Narrow column, keep it short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_DriveHealthWarningTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>El estado de la unidad requiere atención</value>
    <comment>[dialog] Title of the Windows tray balloon notification raised when a drive's SMART health reading turns Warning or Critical. The body is composed at runtime from the drive name and the provider's own message. This warns about hardware condition, not about disk space.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_DrivesHealthy" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Unidades correctas</value>
    <comment>[status] Free-space summary shown in the navigation rail's 'Global status' box and in the top status strip when no drive is anywhere near full. 'Drives' means storage drives/volumes. This is the good-news counterpart of Shell_LowestFreeSpace.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_GlobalStatus" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Estado global</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_LastScan" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Último análisis: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the main window's top status strip. {0} is the root folder path of the most recent scan, for example C:\Users\Ada. The line is trimmed with an ellipsis when it does not fit, so keep the leading label short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_LatestScanUnavailable" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Último análisis no disponible</value>
    <comment>[status] Line in the 'Global status' box at the bottom of the navigation rail. Shown before the most recent scan session has been loaded from the database; replaced once it is. Narrow column (about 270 px), so keep it short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_LowDiskBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>En {0} solo queda un {1}% libre ({2} GB).</value>
    <comment>[dialog] Body of the low-disk-space tray notification. {0} is the drive name as Windows reports it (for example 'C:\'), {1} is the whole-number percentage of free space, {2} is the free space in gigabytes already formatted to one decimal place. Keep all three placeholders and do not renumber them.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_LowDiskTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Poco espacio en disco</value>
    <comment>[dialog] Title of the Windows tray balloon notification raised by the background monitor when a drive drops below the warning or critical free-space threshold. Body text is Shell_LowDiskBody. Windows truncates long notification titles.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_LowestFreeSpace" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Espacio libre mínimo: {0}</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_MonitoringActive" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Supervisión activa</value>
    <comment>[status] Status word in the main window's top status strip, far right. Means the background disk-space monitor is running. Replaced at runtime by Shell_DrivesHealthy or Shell_LowestFreeSpace once the monitor has taken its first reading. Very tight horizontal space - keep it short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_NoScanLoaded" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Sin análisis cargado</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the main window's top status strip, right-aligned next to the product name. Shown before any scan result has been read from the database; replaced at runtime by Shell_LastScan once a scan exists. Very tight horizontal space - keep it short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_NoScansYet" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Aún no hay análisis</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_ScanInProgress" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>en curso</value>
    <comment>[status] Substituted for a completion timestamp in the navigation rail's status line when the most recent scan has not finished. It is appended after the scan status and a middle dot, so it reads like 'Running - in progress'. Lower-case on purpose: it is a sentence fragment, not a standalone label.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_StartScanHint" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Inicie un análisis para generar los datos del espacio de trabajo</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Line in the navigation rail's 'Global status' box when the database holds no scan sessions at all. Tells a first-time user what to do to populate the app. 'Scan' is the noun/verb for indexing a folder tree; 'workspace data' means the indexed results the other pages read from.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_Subtitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Centro de control de almacenamiento v2</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_Tray_Exit" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Salir</value>
    <comment>[button] Last entry in the tray icon's right-click menu, below a separator. Quits the application entirely rather than hiding it back to the notification area. Use the same word Windows uses for quitting an app from a tray menu.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_Tray_NotificationsPausedBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Las notificaciones de poco espacio en disco están pausadas durante 12 horas.</value>
    <comment>[dialog] Body of the confirmation tray notification after the user pauses notifications. States the fixed pause length; the 12 hours is hard-coded, so it is safe to spell out in the translation.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_Tray_NotificationsPausedTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Notificaciones en pausa</value>
    <comment>[dialog] Title of the confirmation tray notification shown immediately after the user picks 'Pause Notifications' from the tray icon's right-click menu. Body is Shell_Tray_NotificationsPausedBody.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_Tray_Open" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Abrir StorageMaster</value>
    <comment>[button] First entry in the tray icon's right-click menu. Restores the main window when the app is minimised to the notification area. 'StorageMaster' is the product name and stays untranslated.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_Tray_PauseNotifications" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Pausar notificaciones</value>
    <comment>[button] Entry in the tray icon's right-click menu. Suppresses low-disk and drive-health tray notifications for 12 hours. Confirmed afterwards by Shell_Tray_NotificationsPausedTitle and Shell_Tray_NotificationsPausedBody.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_Tray_ReviewDuplicates" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Revisar duplicados</value>
    <comment>[button] Entry in the tray icon's right-click menu. Opens the main window on the Duplicates page, where duplicate files found by a scan are listed for review. Nothing is deleted by choosing this.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_Tray_SmartClean" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ejecutar limpieza inteligente</value>
    <comment>[button] Entry in the tray icon's right-click menu. Opens the main window on the Smart Cleaner page - it deletes nothing by itself, the user still reviews and confirms there. 'Smart Clean' is this app's name for the guided cleanup feature and must match the wording used for Nav_SmartCleaner.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_Tray_StartScan" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Iniciar análisis</value>
    <comment>[button] Entry in the tray icon's right-click menu. Opens the main window on the Scan page so the user can start indexing a folder. It does not begin a scan on its own.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Analyse" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Analizar el equipo</value>
    <comment>[button] Primary button in the Smart Cleaner page header. Starts the read-only scan that looks for junk files; it deletes nothing.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_AutomationName" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Página de limpieza inteligente</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader name for the whole Smart Cleaner page (the page reached from the Clean &gt; Smart Cleaner navigation entry). Announced when the page gains focus.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Card_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Eliminación de archivos basura con un solo clic</value>
    <comment>[header] Header of the introduction card on the Smart Cleaner page, next to the page's icon.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_FailureDetails_AuditWarning" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Advertencia de auditoría: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] One entry in the 'Failure and audit details' list on the Smart Cleaner page, reporting that the restore record for a removed item could not be written. {0} is the underlying technical detail, which stays English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_FailureDetails_CleanupError" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error de limpieza: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] One entry in the 'Failure and audit details' list on the Smart Cleaner page, for an error raised during the cleanup. {0} is the underlying technical error text, which stays English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_FailureDetails_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Detalles de errores y auditoría</value>
    <comment>[header] Header of the card on the Smart Cleaner page that lists the individual paths that could not be processed and any audit-record warnings.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_FailureDetails_ScanWarning" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Advertencia del análisis — {0}: {1}</value>
    <comment>[status] One entry in the 'Failure and audit details' list on the Smart Cleaner page, for a path the scan could not inspect. {0} is the path, {1} the underlying technical reason, which stays English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Result_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Resultado de la limpieza</value>
    <comment>[header] Title of the banner that appears on the Smart Cleaner page after a cleanup run. The banner's body is the run's status sentence.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_AwaitingConfirmation" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Esperando la confirmación de la limpieza…</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Smart Cleaner page while the confirmation dialog is open and the app is waiting for the user's answer.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_CancelledNothingRemoved" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Limpieza cancelada antes de eliminar ninguna ruta. Vuelva a analizar antes de intentarlo de nuevo.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line and result banner on the Smart Cleaner page when the run was cancelled before anything was touched.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_CancelledPartial" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Limpieza cancelada tras un progreso parcial. {0} Vuelva a analizar antes de intentarlo de nuevo.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line and result banner on the Smart Cleaner page when a cleanup was cancelled after part of the work was already done. {0} is the whole sentence from Safety_Smart_Summary_RecycleBin or Safety_Smart_Summary_Permanent, so keep a sentence break on both sides of it.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_CancellingCleanup" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cancelando la limpieza…</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Smart Cleaner page between the user pressing Cancel and the running cleanup actually stopping.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_CancellingScan" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cancelando el análisis…</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Smart Cleaner page between the user pressing Cancel and the running scan actually stopping.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_Cleaning" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Limpiando…</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Smart Cleaner page while the confirmed cleanup is running.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_CleanupCancelled" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Limpieza cancelada. Vuelva a analizar antes de intentarlo de nuevo, porque el estado de los archivos puede haber cambiado.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Smart Cleaner page after the user cancelled a cleanup that had already started. Part of the files may already be gone, so a fresh scan is required.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_CleanupFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error en la limpieza. Vuelva a analizar antes de intentarlo de nuevo, porque el estado de los archivos puede haber cambiado.</value>
