  <data name="Workspace_Duplicates_Summary" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} grupos · {1}</value>
    <comment>[status] Summary of the latest duplicate detection run, shown in the Scan Workspace review-queue card and on the Duplicates tab. {0} is the number of duplicate groups found, pre-formatted with thousands separators; a group is one set of identical files. {1} is the run's state (an internal English word such as Completed). The separator is a middle dot.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Duplicates_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Revisión de duplicados</value>
    <comment>[title] Heading of the placeholder on the Duplicates tab of the Scan Workspace, above a button that opens the duplicates page. Means the step where the user goes through duplicate files and decides which copies to keep.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Metric_Errors" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Errores</value>
    <comment>[label] Label of a readout card on the Scan Workspace page. The value below is how many paths the scanner could not read. Plural noun.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Metric_Files" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Archivos</value>
    <comment>[label] Label of a readout card on the Scan Workspace page. The value below is how many files the scan found. Plural noun.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Metric_Folders" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Carpetas</value>
    <comment>[label] Label of a readout card on the Scan Workspace page. The value below is how many folders the scan found. Plural noun.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Metric_ScannedSize" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Tamaño analizado</value>
    <comment>[label] Label of the first readout card on the Scan Workspace page. The value below is the combined size of everything this scan covered.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Overview_Composition" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Composición por tipo de archivo</value>
    <comment>[header] Heading of the card on the Scan Workspace Overview tab that breaks the scan down by file category, showing how much of the scanned data each category accounts for.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Overview_ReviewQueue" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cola de revisión</value>
    <comment>[header] Heading of the card on the Scan Workspace Overview tab that summarises what is waiting for the user's review: duplicate findings and how much space could be recovered.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Page_AutomationName" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Página del espacio de trabajo de análisis</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader name for the whole Scan Workspace page, announced when it is opened. Not visible on screen.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Reclaimable_Idle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ejecute una limpieza o una revisión de duplicados para estimar el espacio recuperable.</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Helper line in the Scan Workspace review-queue card before anything has been analysed. Tells the user which two actions produce an estimate of how much space could be freed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Reclaimable_NoRun" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ejecute una revisión de duplicados para estimar el espacio recuperable.</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Helper line in the Scan Workspace review-queue card when the scan loaded but no duplicate run exists for it yet.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Reclaimable_Summary" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} recuperables de la última detección de duplicados.</value>
    <comment>[status] Helper line in the Scan Workspace review-queue card. {0} is a data size, already formatted (for example '2.3 GB'), that could be freed by removing redundant copies found in the most recent duplicate run. Nothing is deleted by this text.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_SpaceMap_Action" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Abrir Mapa de espacio</value>
    <comment>[button] Button on the Space Map tab of the Scan Workspace that navigates to the Space Map page for this scan. Same English text as the heading above it, but this one is the button.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_SpaceMap_Message" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>El treemap interactivo se abre con el contexto de este análisis y sigue encauzando las acciones destructivas a través de los flujos de revisión.</value>
    <comment>[description] Explanatory text on the Space Map tab of the Scan Workspace. Says that opening the Space Map carries this scan's data over, and that anything which deletes files there still goes through a review step first rather than acting immediately.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_SpaceMap_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Abrir Mapa de espacio</value>
    <comment>[title] Heading of the placeholder shown on the Space Map tab of the Scan Workspace, above a button that opens the Space Map page. 'Space Map' is the app's interactive treemap view of disk usage.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Status_IncompleteScan" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Este análisis está en estado {0}. Los datos parciales del análisis están ocultos; complete un análisis nuevo antes de abrir Resultados, Limpieza, Duplicados o Mapa de espacio.</value>
    <comment>[status] Information bar on the Scan Workspace page for a scan that did not finish. {0} is its state (an internal English word such as Failed or Cancelled). Explains that half-finished numbers are deliberately withheld and lists four pages of the app the user should not open until a new scan has run.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Status_LoadFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No se pudo cargar el espacio de trabajo: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Information bar on the Scan Workspace page when opening the page threw an error. {0} is the technical error text and stays in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Status_Loaded" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Datos del espacio de trabajo cargados desde un análisis completado y guardado.</value>
    <comment>[status] Information bar at the bottom of the Scan Workspace page once everything has been read successfully from a finished, stored scan.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Status_Loading" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cargando los datos del análisis guardado...</value>
    <comment>[status] Information bar at the bottom of the Scan Workspace page while the stored scan is being read from the app's database. 'persisted' means saved from an earlier run. Ends with three plain full stops in the English original.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Status_NoCompletedScans" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No hay ningún análisis completado disponible.</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Shown as both the subtitle and the information bar on the Scan Workspace page when the app holds no finished scan at all.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Status_ScannerReport" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Informe del analizador: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Appended to Workspace_Status_IncompleteScan, after a space, when the scanner recorded why it stopped. {0} is the scanner's own message and stays in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Status_SelectScan" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Seleccione un análisis completado.</value>
    <comment>[status] Text of the information bar at the bottom of the Scan Workspace page before any scan is loaded. Imperative.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Status_SessionUnavailable" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>La sesión de análisis solicitada no está disponible.</value>
    <comment>[status] Shown as both the subtitle and the information bar on the Scan Workspace page when the scan the user navigated to no longer exists. 'session' means one scan run.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Summary_Loading" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cargando la sesión de análisis...</value>
    <comment>[status] Subtitle under the Scan Workspace heading while the scan record is being read. 'session' means one scan run. Ends with three plain full stops in the English original.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Summary_NoScan" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ningún análisis seleccionado.</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Subtitle under the Scan Workspace heading before any scan has been chosen.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Summary_StatusStarted" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} · iniciado el {1}</value>
    <comment>[status] Subtitle under the Scan Workspace heading once a scan is loaded. {0} is the scan's state (an internal English word such as Completed or Failed, not translated), {1} the local date and time the scan began, already formatted. The separator is a middle dot.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Tab_Delta" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Comparación</value>
    <comment>[header] Tab of the Scan Workspace page about what changed between two comparable scans of the same folder.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Tab_Errors" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Errores</value>
    <comment>[header] Tab of the Scan Workspace page listing paths the scanner could not read. Plural noun.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Tab_Files" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Archivos</value>
    <comment>[header] Tab of the Scan Workspace page listing the scan's largest individual files. Plural noun.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Tab_Folders" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Carpetas</value>
    <comment>[header] Tab of the Scan Workspace page listing the scan's largest folders. Plural noun.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Tab_Overview" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Vista general</value>
    <comment>[header] First tab of the Scan Workspace page, holding the file-type breakdown and the review queue.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Espacio de trabajo de análisis</value>
    <comment>[title] Heading of the Scan Workspace page while no particular scan is loaded. The Scan Workspace gathers one scan's overview, files, folders, duplicates and errors on a single page.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Title_ForRoot" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Análisis: {0}</value>
    <comment>[title] Heading of the Scan Workspace page once a scan is loaded. {0} is the folder or drive path that was scanned.</comment>
  </data>
</root>
